<urn:atm:triage:finding/BB3-022>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "BB3-022" ;
  triage:title "Two Python smoke-runner files exceed 1000 lines -- advisory, RULE-003's actual gate never scans Python" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr BB3-QA3-1789250000 (Final verdict FAIL, https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1445#issuecomment-5648698551, 2026-09-12T21:08:20Z; BB3-QA3-M6), reviewed at 66be1d012. scripts/smoke/run_admission_capacity.py (2444 lines) and scripts/smoke/run_feature_smoke.py (1110 lines) both exceed 1000 lines, but confirmed .just/check_line_counts.py (the actual RULE-003 gate behind just lint lines, per project_rule003_authoritative_gate) only scans Rust crate src/**/*.rs, never Python -- so AC6 is unaffected. Advisory decomposition debt only, not a gate failure." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-bb" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "maintainability" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:source "qa" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "scripts/smoke/run_admission_capacity.py,scripts/smoke/run_feature_smoke.py" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-12T21:08:20Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "Advisory only -- no gate is failing. Consider decomposition in a future sweep if these files continue to grow. Routed to solar's BB3-FIX-R3-1789253000 (fenix, promote_to_branch fix/bb3-qa3-r3, queued behind BB1-FIX-R1) for visibility, not a required fix in this round. cipher's BB3-FIX-R4-1789255000 (task event 2026-09-12T23:08:15Z) fixed this on fix/bb3-qa3-r4 @ f94125cf5 (PR #1455, includes merges of #1456 d1969185f and #1453 1c7e76da5); just lint 36/36, just test exit 0, just smoke fast 8/8. Fixed-pending-QA; QA dispatched as BB3-QA4-1789262000 on PR #1455 (queued behind BB5-QA-R1). STILL OPEN, severity raised minor->blocking (BB3-QA4-1789262000, PR #1455 comment, 2026-09-12T23:24:52Z, per arch-qa's specialist-reviewer judgment as an architectural RULE-003 principle regardless of the Rust-only CI gate's scope; req-qa rated the same fact Minor, reported at the higher specialist severity): the split introduced a globals().update({{name: getattr(module, name) for name in module.__all__}}) immediately after import, plus module._PUBLIC_NAMESPACE = globals() handing the caller's own globals back to the split module so its functions indirect through a _public(name, fallback) lookup (12 call sites in admission_capacity_support.py alone) into the original file's namespace -- a re-export-everything-back shim creating circular runtime coupling, not a real module boundary. admission_capacity_support.py itself is 1659/1473 non-blank lines, over the 1000-line target that motivated the split. Next: replace the globals().update()/_PUBLIC_NAMESPACE circular-injection pattern in both split pairs with explicit function parameters or an injected context object, and split admission_capacity_support.py further so every resulting file is genuinely under 1000 lines. Cut on a new layer above fix/bb3-qa3-r4 (top of stack #1457). Corrected routing (fenix, 2026-09-12T23:32:13Z): the fix layer is fix/bb3-qa4-r5, cut from a7d4664d1 (feature/bb6-storage-prompt-handoffs, top of stack #1457) -- not directly above fix/bb3-qa3-r4. In the BB3-FIX-R5-1789264000 fence, closes on cipher's fix. cipher's BB3 R5 final push landed at fix/bb3-qa4-r5 @ 5da523f81 (parent merge-forward 16f2ab124), 2026-09-13T00:45:41Z, self-reported fresh just smoke fast 8/8, evidence archived outside tree, reports index unchanged. Fixed-pending-QA. Per cipher's task-close (relayed by fenix, 2026-09-13T00:52:35Z), this finding's fix landed at f6214af22. QA-R5 dispatched (BB3-QA-R5-1789273000) on PR #1463 @ 5da523f81, frozen, base ref for the diff 40ccd403e." ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BB3 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-12T21:08:20Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
